# Test requests for the course, in chapter order.
#
# Run them in IntelliJ IDEA (built-in HTTP Client) or VS Code (REST Client extension):
# open this file and click the run icon next to a request.
#
# Start LM Studio first. Start the app with ./gradlew bootRun (port 8080).
# The replies shown in the comments come from one run with Gemma. Your wording will differ.
#
# Watch the app console after each request. The "Log:" lines below say what to look for.
# Chapter 2, Table 2.1 explains each log tag.

@lmstudio = http://localhost:1234/v1
@app = http://localhost:8080


### Chapter 2 · List the model identifiers in LM Studio
# Each model name in application.yaml must match an "id" here.
GET {{lmstudio}}/models


### Chapter 2 · Pre-flight: Gemma must return a tool call
# Expect "finish_reason": "tool_calls" and a countErrors call with service "checkout".
# If the reply has no tool_calls, do not start Chapter 3.
POST {{lmstudio}}/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "google/gemma-4-12b-qat",
  "messages": [
    {"role": "user", "content": "How many error events in the checkout service in the last 15 minutes?"}
  ],
  "tools": [
    {
      "type": "function",
      "function": {
        "name": "countErrors",
        "description": "Count error log events for one service in the last N minutes.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "service": {"type": "string"},
            "minutes": {"type": "integer"}
          },
          "required": ["service", "minutes"]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}


### Chapter 3 · One model call, no tools
# Expect the model to ask for logs: it has no data yet.
# After Chapter 4 the same request runs the tool instead.
# Log: [auto] ... then Chat Model Prompt Content with 2 messages. No "Executing tool call" line.
GET {{app}}/askAutoToolCall?input=how many error events?


### Chapter 4 · No service name: the model asks for one
# Expect: "Please specify which service you would like to check ..."
# Log: one model call, no "Executing tool call" line. The model asked instead of guessing.
GET {{app}}/askAutoToolCall?input=how many error events?


### Chapter 4 · Search service: the fake data returns 3
# Expect: "There were 3 error events in the search service in the last 10 minutes."
GET {{app}}/askAutoToolCall?input=how many error events in search service?


### Chapter 4 · Checkout service: the fake data returns 412
# Gemma sometimes asks for a time window instead. Add "in the last 15 minutes" to the question if it does.
# Expect: "There were 412 error events in the checkout service in the last 15 minutes."
# Log: [auto], then DefaultToolCallingManager "Executing tool call: countErrors": Spring AI ran the tool.
#      [tool] countErrors(service=checkout, ...) returned 412, then a second model call.
GET {{app}}/askAutoToolCall?input=how many error events in checkout service?


### Chapter 5 · Step 1: halt the tool call
# Expect one tool call, unrun:
# [{"id":"...","type":"function","name":"countErrors","arguments":"{\"minutes\":60,\"service\":\"checkout\"}"}]
# Log: [halt] Model requested countErrors {...}. Not run.  No [tool] line: nothing ran.
GET {{app}}/askHaltToolCall?input=how many error events in checkout service?


### Chapter 5 · Step 1: no tool needed
# Expect: []
# Log: [halt] Model answered in text, with no tool call: ...
GET {{app}}/askHaltToolCall?input=what is a harness?


### Chapter 5 · Step 4: run the loop
# Expect: {"answer":"There were 412 error events ...","reason":"FINAL_ANSWER","steps":2,"tokens":727}
# Log: [loop] Step 1/5: sending 2 messages ... your code runs countErrors ... [tool] ... returned 412
#      [loop] Step 2/5: sending 4 messages ... Stop: FINAL_ANSWER.  No "Executing tool call" line:
#      your loop ran the tool, not Spring AI.
GET {{app}}/run?input=how many error events in checkout service?


### Chapter 5 · Step 4: two tool calls in one step
# Expect: {"answer":"Checkout is significantly worse ... 412 ... 3 ...","reason":"FINAL_ANSWER","steps":2,"tokens":480}
# Log: [loop] Step 1: model requested 2 tool call(s), then one "your code runs" line per service.
GET {{app}}/run?input=is checkout or search worse right now?


### Chapter 5 · Step 4: no service name
# Expect a question back in one step: {"answer":"Please specify which service ...","reason":"FINAL_ANSWER","steps":1,...}
# Log: [loop] Step 1: no tool calls. Stop: FINAL_ANSWER
GET {{app}}/run?input=how many error events?


### Chapter 6 · Step 3: the stop-reason test
# Send this request once per row below. Change one constant in AgentLoop.java,
# restart (or rebuild with DevTools), send, then put the constant back.
#
#   no change                          -> FINAL_ANSWER   steps 2
#   MAX_STEPS = 1                      -> STEP_LIMIT     steps 1, answer null
#   MAX_TOKENS = 100                   -> TOKEN_BUDGET   steps 1, answer null
#   TIMEOUT = Duration.ofMillis(1)     -> TIMEOUT        steps 1, answer null
#   MAX_REPEATS = 1                    -> LOOP_DETECTED  steps 1, answer null
#
# Log: each early stop prints its reason before any tool runs, for example
#      [loop] Step 1: 237 tokens is over MAX_TOKENS 100. Stop: TOKEN_BUDGET
#
# Keep the time window in the question. Without it, Gemma can ask for the window in text,
# which ends the run as FINAL_ANSWER before any limit fires.
GET {{app}}/run?input=how many error events in the checkout service in the last 15 minutes?
